We are seeking an experienced and reliable Window Fitter to join our team in Galway. The successful candidate will be responsible for fitting, repairing and replacing glass installations in residential and commercial properties while ensuring high standards of workmanship and safety.

Key Duties and Responsibilities:
Examines drawings and specifications to determine job requirements and measurements;
Measures, cuts and prepares plain, coloured, safety and ornamental glass for installation;
Smoothes and finishes glass edges and positions glass securely into frames or grooved lead strips;
Applies mastic, putty or adhesive between glass and frames and removes excess material for a clean finish;
Installs mirror panels on interior and exterior walls;
Repairs and replaces damaged or broken glass panels and fittings;
Ensures all fitting and glazing work is completed in accordance with safety standards and company procedures.

Requirements:
Previous experience as a Window Fitter, Glazier or similar role;
Ability to read technical drawings and specifications;
Good manual dexterity and attention to detail;
Knowledge of glass fitting materials, tools and installation techniques;
Ability to work independently and as part of a team;
Good communication skills and strong work ethic.

Employment Type: Full-time, Permanent
Salary: Competitive salary depending on experience.

In order to work in Ireland a non-EEA National, unless they are exempted, must hold a valid employment permit.  Please review the Eligibility and requirements for an employment permit if you are unsure of your eligibility to apply for this vacancy. <br>  Outlined Beauty is looking for a skilled and passionate Digital Marketing Executive to join our team, drive revenue growth, and strengthen client relationships. This role is crucial in driving business growth, expanding our market presence, and delivering outstanding customer service. 

Key responsibilities:
Discusses business methods, products or services and targets customer group with employer or client in order to identify marketing requirements;
Establishes an appropriate quantitative and qualitative market research methodology and prepares proposals outlining programmes of work and details of costs;
Collates and interprets findings of market research and presents results to clients;
Discusses possible changes that need to be made in terms of design, price, packaging, promotion etc. in light of market research with appropriate departments;
Briefs advertising team on client requirements, monitors the progress of advertising campaigns and liaises with client on potential modifications;
Discusses employer’s or clients’ requirements, plans and monitors surveys and analyses of customers’ reactions to products;
Produces and/or assesses reports and recommendations concerning marketing and sales strategies;
Maintain relationships with customers to encourage referrals and ensure a 5-star experience;
Created and optimize content for social media, website, and email marketing, driving engagement and brand awareness; 
Leading sales and marketing strategies, achieving revenue growth through data-driven decision-making. 


Qualifications: 
Proven experience (1+ years) as a Sales Executive, Marketing Executive or similar role. 
Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build relationships with clients at all levels. 
Fluent in Portuguese (Brazilian) as most of the clients are Brazilians.
Excellent negotiation and presentation skills, with a customer-focused approach to sales. 
Self-motivated, goal-oriented, and capable of working independently as well as part of a team. 
Ability to analyze market trends and adapt sales strategies accordingly. 
Some experience in leading websites;

Work Location: Mayor Street Lower, Dublin
Work Pattern: Daytime / Morning &amp; Afternoon availability, Monday – Saturday (5 days) 39 hours a week

